sequenceDiagram
    participant Scheduler as Background Scheduler
    participant ExpiryJob as IdentifierExpirationJob
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Log as ECS JSON log

    Note over Scheduler: Scheduled task runs daily at a randomised time 03:45–05:45 local<br/>(load spread across EU gates). Configurable via IDENTIFIER_EXPIRY_CRON.

    Scheduler->>+ExpiryJob: triggerExpiryJob()
    ExpiryJob->>+Log: INSERT INTO jobs_execution_log (job_name, started_at, status='running')

    ExpiryJob->>+DB: SELECT dataset_id FROM consignments<br/>WHERE status='active' AND mode='road'<br/>AND transport_date + INTERVAL '14 days' < NOW()
    Note over DB: Uses idx_consignments_expires_at (partial index<br/>on status='active' AND expires_at IS NOT NULL).<br/>Cabotage retention per Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4).
    DB-->>-ExpiryJob: [550e8400-…, a1b2c3d4-…, c3d4e5f6-…]

    loop For each expired road consignment
        ExpiryJob->>+DB: UPDATE consignments<br/>SET status='inactive'<br/>WHERE dataset_id='550e8400-…' AND status='active'
        DB-->>-ExpiryJob: 1 row updated
        Note over DB: AFTER UPDATE trigger consignments_change_history<br/>writes (table='consignments', row_id='550e8400-…',<br/>column='status', old='active', new='inactive') to change_history.
        ExpiryJob->>Log: { event.action: "identifier.expire",<br/>efti.dataset.id: "550e8400-…", efti.expiry.reason: "cabotage_14d" }
    end

    ExpiryJob->>+DB: UPDATE jobs_execution_log<br/>SET finished_at=NOW(), status='completed',<br/>details=jsonb_build_object('expired_count', 3)
    DB-->>-ExpiryJob: ok
    ExpiryJob-->>-Scheduler: done

    Note over Scheduler: Non-road modes (maritime/rail/air/multimodal)<br/>are NOT expired by this job — Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4)<br/>cabotage retention applies to road only.
